The class DefaultRespCommandsDataProvider<TData> is internal and inaccessible for direct use in tests. However, the public factory RespCommandsDataProviderFactory provides an instance of IRespCommandsDataProvider<TData> which we can use to call TryImportRespCommandsData. This interface is public, so we can use it in the test.

I will rewrite the test to get the provider instance from RespCommandsDataProviderFactory.GetRespCommandsDataProvider<TestCommandData>() and then call TryImportRespCommandsData on that instance. This avoids accessing the internal class directly.

I will also fix the logger verification to use the correct LogError extension method signature with Moq.

